# فایل کامل README.md

در ادامه، محتوای کامل فایل `README.md` به‌صورت یکجا آمده است. کل بلوک زیر را کپی کنید و در فایل `README.md` در ریشه‌ی مخزن ذخیره کنید.

```markdown
# TOPTrust: Topology-Aware Differentially Private Federated Learning for Misbehavior Detection in VANETs

[![Python 3.10+](https://img.shields.io/badge/python-3.10%2B-blue.svg)](https://www.python.org/)
[![PyTorch](https://img.shields.io/badge/PyTorch-2.x-red.svg)](https://pytorch.org/)
[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](LICENSE)

A reference implementation of **TOPTrust**, a federated learning framework with
**client-level differential privacy (DP)** for detecting misbehaving vehicles in
Vehicular Ad-Hoc Networks (VANETs). The method combines:

- A **temporal graph neural network** with a learnable global time-decay coefficient.
- **Topology-aware clipping** for heterogeneous vehicle degrees.
- **Hierarchical aggregation** (vehicle -> RSU -> TA).
- **RDP accounting** for the Poisson-subsampled Gaussian mechanism.
- A **bootstrap** module for cold-start vehicles.

> **Privacy scope.** Finite-epsilon guarantees are certified **only** for the `uniform`
> clipping mode under client-level add/remove-one adjacency, a fixed public client
> universe, Poisson sampling, and a single server-side Gaussian perturbation. Other
> clipping modes (`topology`, `privatized`) are provided for **non-private ablations**
> and must be run with `--epsilon inf`.

> **Data scope.** The repository ships with a synthetic generator. The InTAS adapter
> uses the official Train/Validation/Test split shipped with the dataset. VeReMi is
> optional and loaded from a user-supplied directory.

---

